and finishing workflows. Sapphire supports industry-standard hosts including Adobe After Effects, Adobe Premiere Pro, Avid Media Composer, DaVinci Resolve, Foundry Nuke, Autodesk Flame, VEGAS Pro, Blackmagic Fusion Studio, and other OFX-compatible applications. Sapphire runs on macOS, Windows, and Linux and features GPU acceleration across all platforms (Nvidia, AMD, and Apple Silicon). Originally launched in 1996, Sapphire has been a standard in professional post-production for nearly 30 years, and is the recipient of a 2019 Primetime Engineering Emmy Award. The suite includes advanced lens flares, glows, light effects, blurs, film looks, stylize effects, transitions, distortions, and texture generators, along with integrated Mocha planar tracking and masking for advanced compositing workflows. Sapphire is used by professional editors, VFX artists, colorists, motion designers, broadcasters, and content creators for cinematic visual effects, motion design, broadcast graphics, music videos, commercial finishing, and social media content. Sapphire has been used on major productions including The Lord of the Rings films (Wētā FX), Star Wars (Industrial Light and Magic), and Game of Thrones (Pixomondo). \"","url":"\"https://borisfx.com/products/sapphire/\"","image":"\"https://borisfx-com-res.cloudinary.com/image/upload/v1772150946/Marketing/2026%20Logos/Sapphire/Horizontal/Light/SVG/Sapphire_Horizontal.svg\"","softwareVersion":"2026.5","publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Boris FX","url":"https://borisfx.com"},"offers":[{"@type":"Offer","name":"Adobe/OFX Monthly Subscription","price":"80.00","priceCurrency":"USD"},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Adobe/OFX Annual Subscription","price":"545.00","priceCurrency":"USD"},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Adobe/OFX Perpetual License","price":"1865.00","priceCurrency":"USD"},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Avid-only Monthly Subscription","price":"80.00","priceCurrency":"USD"},{"@type":"Offer","name":"Avid-only Annual Subscription","price":"545